{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Then</b> — Some say: <b>ידבר</b> is like <b>יאבד</b>, like <b>ותדבר את כל זרע המלוכה</b> [and she destroyed all the royal seed], which is an expression of death, like <b>אהי דברך מות</b> [let your word be death]. Like <b>ותדבר את כל זרע המלוכה</b>, for it is written in another book <b>ותדבר</b>, from the root דבר, very heavy." "<b>אלימו</b> — the strong ones, like <b>ואת אילי הארץ לקח</b> [and he took the rams of the earth]. This is not correct, for <b>אילי הארץ</b> is on the pattern of <b>אבירי בשן</b>, and it is with yod, for it is from the root איל. The correct view: <b>ידבר</b> in its plain sense, and <b>אלימו</b> like <b>אליהם</b> [to them], and <b>עלימו</b> like <b>עליהם</b> [upon them]. Thus <b>ידבר אליהם</b> [he speaks to them]: <b>למה רגשו גוים</b> [Why do the nations rage]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The comment is textually repetitive, citing ותדבר את כל זרע המלוכה twice; translated as received without smoothing. 'ספר אחר' likely refers to a variant Masoretic reading or a parallel version of the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:21.075272168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}